TITLE:: ParaEQView
summary:: the response curve of an eq, and its handles
categories:: Libraries>ParaEQ
related:: Classes/ParaEQ, Classes/ParaEQPanel, Classes/ParaEQSpectrum

DESCRIPTION::
The five bands as five dots on a frequency / gain plane, over the curve they add
up to, each band's own share filled under it. Behind them, when the view has
been given a link::Classes/ParaEQSpectrum::, the spectrum of what the eq is
working on. This is the middle of link::Classes/ParaEQPanel::; a window that
wants only the curve can make one on its own.

code::
v = ParaEQView(parent);
v.eq = someParaEQ;
v.spectrum = ParaEQSpectrum(someParaEQ);
::

definitionList::
## drag || frequency and gain of the nearest band - a dot never has to be hit exactly
## cmd + drag up / down || the width of the emphasis::selected:: band, from wherever you press. code::alt:: does the same
## the wheel || the width again
## shift while dragging || snap to round frequencies, whole dB, round widths
## double click a dot || that band back to 0 dB
::

The width drag is relative - it starts from the width the band already has
rather than from where the mouse landed - so it never jumps on the first pixel.

The curve is worked out from the same coefficients the server runs, see
link::Classes/ParaEQ#*coeffs::, and kept between redraws: with an analyser
running the view redraws twenty times a second.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
ARGUMENT:: parent
ARGUMENT:: bounds

METHOD:: grabRadius
How near a dot a double click has to land. 10.

METHOD:: widthPerPixel
How much of the width one pixel of a cmd drag is worth. 1.02.

METHOD:: freqSnap
METHOD:: shelfQSnap
METHOD:: peakQSnap
What shift snaps to.

METHOD:: isWidthMod
Which modifier keys mean "width, not position".

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: view
The link::Classes/UserView::.

METHOD:: eq
The link::Classes/ParaEQ:: drawn.

METHOD:: spectrum
A link::Classes/ParaEQSpectrum::, or nil for the curve alone.

METHOD:: selected
The band being worked on. Setting it from outside reaches the panel's number
boxes too.

METHOD:: action
Called with the view and code::\select:: when the selection changes.

METHOD:: refresh
